35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found that only two firms can do the big digging. They are worried about the clay.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,I see. The habitat fund only pays for plants and water. It does not cover the paving.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That is a problem. The old basin is fine, but the apron outside the hall is patched.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The staff roll is down to seven. But there are two volunteer groups ready to help.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The counts show people want firm ground. The drainage calls have doubled since the cap.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, if the fund doesn't cover paving, that changes the budget significantly.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, yes. And the upkeep for planted ground is triple the cost of hard surfaces.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,That explains why the trees died. No one was paid to water them properly.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"The volunteers can help with the habitat, but they cannot fix the drainage or the heat.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,The heat is a real issue. The readings are much higher here than on the shaded streets.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"The phasing notes say we can hoard the south, but not the center. That limits our options.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,So we cannot build a big plaza in the middle without extra cost. The fund won't cover it.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"We need to be realistic. If we plant, we must pay for the care. It is not cheap.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"The volunteers are good for the edges, but the core needs professional attention.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"We need a plan that works with the ground, not against it. The clay is a constraint.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think we need to be careful with the earth-moving. It is risky and expensive.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,I agree. The long-term costs are the real test. We cannot afford to be surprised.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us look at what has worked before. The basin is a good example of durability.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"The volunteers are a resource, but they are not a replacement for staff.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,The data is clear. We need to manage the water and the heat. That is the priority.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
