60,3,1,talk,Minato,,I am leaning towards the Wetland Restoration. It uses the water we have and avoids the clay issues.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,I am worried about the cost. The upkeep for water and plants is high. But the fund helps.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The Wetland plan seems to learn from the past. It manages the water, which is our biggest problem.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,The volunteers can help with the habitat tasks. It fits with what they are already doing.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,The drainage calls are up. The Wetland plan addresses that directly. It is the logical choice.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, yes, the drainage is the key. The other plans ignore it.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, I agree. The fund covers the water management. It is the only plan that fits the funding.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,The other plans require too much hard surface. That is expensive to maintain and patch.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,The Sports Terraces would need a lot of turf care. We do not have the staff for that.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,The Market Plaza is a bad idea. The ground is not stable enough for heavy structures.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"The Woodland Walk is nice, but the trees might die again if we do not have the budget for care.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,Exactly. The upkeep ledger shows the cost of planted ground is triple. We cannot afford that without the fund.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,The Wetland plan is more resilient. It works with the natural drainage.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,The volunteers are already working on habitat upriver. This would extend that work.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,The heat readings are high. The water in the Wetland plan would help cool the area.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I am convinced. The Wetland Restoration is the best fit for the site and the constraints.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,I agree. It is the only plan that aligns with the funding and the long-term costs.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I support it. It is a sensible, durable choice.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I am in favor. It leverages the volunteer groups and addresses the drainage.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for D. It is the rational choice based on the data.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
